VeridianOS: registry_p.cpp without unused parameter names, all roles mapped

The D-Bus event slots keep the signature of the AT-SPI signals they are
connected to, but most use only some of the parameters; the others are
now unnamed (in comments, as the file already does for some), so GCC no
longer reports each as unused (-Wunused-parameter, 85 times).
slotPropertyChange() keeps its four names, marked [[maybe_unused]],
because its #ifdef ATSPI_DEBUG trace reads them.

atspiRoleToRole maps the AT-SPI roles that have an AccessibleObject
counterpart; the rest (commented out in the switch, and roles newer
AT-SPI versions added) reached the NoRole return after the switch without
a case, which GCC reports for each enumerator (-Wswitch, 58 times). A
default case now says so; the result is the same.

--- a/src/qaccessibilityclient/registry_p.cpp
+++ b/src/qaccessibilityclient/registry_p.cpp
@@ -697,6 +697,9 @@
 //    case ATSPI_ROLE_NOTIFICATION: return AccessibleObject::;
 //    case ATSPI_ROLE_INFO_BAR: return AccessibleObject::;
 //    case ATSPI_ROLE_LAST_DEFINED: return AccessibleObject::;
+    default:
+        // The roles above without a counterpart, and roles AT-SPI added later.
+        break;
     }
     return AccessibleObject::NoRole;
 }
@@ -1307,92 +1310,92 @@
     return accessibleFromPath(QDBusContext::message().service(), QDBusContext::message().path());
 }
 
